From 7bad4e91126bf7e3b00da5400db6b099711c2c6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leek <liumaoqi@bupt.edu.cn>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 20:27:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [distill] feat: add a generalized-JSD top-k distillation loss

Distillation currently offers forward KL on the teacher's top-k support, plus
the single-sample estimators. This adds the generalized Jensen-Shannon
divergence of Agarwal et al. (GKD, arXiv:2306.13649) as a second top-k loss.

`jsd_beta` interpolates the two directed divergences -- 0 is forward
KL(teacher||student), 1 is reverse KL(student||teacher), and values in between
weight the mixture -- so `generalized_jsd_topk` at beta=0 reproduces the
existing loss and the interesting settings live in between. `jsd_token_clip`
optionally bounds each vocabulary entry's contribution before the sum, which
keeps one very confident teacher id from dominating a token's gradient.
`kd_temperature` applies to both distributions before the divergence;
forward_kl_topk keeps requiring 1.0 because its mass diagnostics assume an
untempered partition.

Selecting a second top-k loss needs a small dispatch: compute_topk_loss hard-
coded compute_forward_kl_topk for every mode, so the backend kernel is now
looked up by loss_mode through TOPK_KERNEL_BY_LOSS_MODE, with the forward-KL
kernel as the fallback every existing mode keeps getting.

Tests pin the maths rather than the implementation: beta=0 and beta=1 equal the
two KLs, beta=0.5 equals the closed-form JSD and is symmetric under swapping the
arguments, the divergence is zero on identical distributions and bounded by
log 2, clipping lowers the loss and reports the clipped fraction, and gradients
reach the student while the teacher term stays detached.

Megatron keeps the forward-KL kernel; a megatron implementation can register
itself in the same map. The student/teacher union support this loss also
supports in a research fork needs an actor-side top-k transport and will be a
separate PR.
